# Enterprise & products imports files
imports/imports.go

# go.work is TRACKED here, and that is the difference between a fork and the
# project it forks. Upstream publishes server/public as a module and pins a
# released version of it, so a workspace is a developer's local convenience and
# belongs in this file. We changed server/public — the Hanzo model lives there —
# so for this tree the workspace is not a convenience, it is the build
# definition: without it every consumer compiles against the published v0.4.0 and
# cannot see our own types.
#
# Tracking it puts that fact in ONE place. `go build`, `go test`, CI's gate and
# the image build each used to arrange the workspace for themselves, and the one
# that did not — the CI gate — failed with "build failed" on symbols that are
# right here on disk.

